{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mr5qowv3GMCUcZDaYZVgHn","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (32.4KB). Full output saved to: /capture/claude-config/projects/-workspace-project/86601755-4788-4419-8422-87dd30678fd9/tool-results/bx8b4g10h.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\nREADME.md\napps\ndb.json\neslint.config.mjs\nnode_modules\nnx.json\npackage.json\npnpm-lock.yaml\npnpm-workspace.yaml\nspec\ntsconfig.base.json\n# Cinescope — cinema seat booking\n\nA web application for booking cinema seats. A customer picks a day and a movie screening,\nchooses seats on a map of the auditorium, reviews the tickets, fills in their details and\npays.\n\nThis file is the complete specification. The work is split into tickets in\n[`tickets/`](tickets/README.md); each ticket points back to the sections below and lists\nthe acceptance criteria it has to satisfy.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project setup\n\nThe framework, the libraries and the state of the scaffold are described in\n[`stack.md`](stack.md). The application is the Nx project `cinescope` in `apps/cinescope`.\n\nAll commands run from the workspace root:\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `pnpm install` | installs dependencies (already done) |\n| `pnpm nx serve cinescope` | starts the application at `http://localhost:4200` |\n| `pnpm api` | starts the backend at `http://localhost:3000` |\n| `pnpm nx build cinescope` | production build — must succeed |\n| `pnpm nx test cinescope` | unit tests (Vitest) |\n| `pnpm nx lint cinescope` | ESLint |\n\nRules for the environment:\n\n- The package manager is pnpm. Do not use `npm` or `yarn`.\n- The application is served at `http://localhost:4200`. Do not change the port.\n- Do not add dependencies. Everything the application needs is already installed.\n- Do not edit `db.json` by hand. It is the backend's data.\n- The application is desktop-only (viewport 1280 × 720 or larger). All user-facing text is\n  in English.\n\n###